/*!
\page page_stmwctriggerdetector StMwcTriggerDetector

\brief MWC trigger detector data: MIP counts for 24 sectors × 4 sub-sectors × 11 time samples.

\section stmwctriggerdetector_overview Overview
\c StMwcTriggerDetector stores data from the Multi-Wire Chamber (MWC), an outer
tracker used in early STAR running.  MIP counts are stored per sector, sub-sector,
and time sample, along with auxiliary DSM words.  MWC data were combined with CTB
data in the L0 DSMs to form combined multiplicity and topology trigger inputs.

\section stmwctriggerdetector_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
TObject
 └── StObject
      └── StMwcTriggerDetector
\endcode

\section stmwctriggerdetector_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| Float_t[24][4][11] | mMips | MIP counts [sector][sub-sector][time sample] |
| Float_t[32][11] | mAux | Auxiliary DSM words [word][time sample] |

\section stmwctriggerdetector_methods Key Methods

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `float mips(int sector, int subsec, int evt=0) const` | MIP count |
| `float aux(int i, int evt=0) const` | Auxiliary word i at sample evt |
| `int numberOfSectors() const` | 24 |
| `int numberOfSubSectors() const` | 4 |

\section stmwctriggerdetector_usage Usage Example
\code{.cpp}
StMwcTriggerDetector& mwc = event->triggerDetectorCollection()->mwc();
for (int s = 0; s < mwc.numberOfSectors(); ++s)
    for (int ss = 0; ss < mwc.numberOfSubSectors(); ++ss)
        if (mwc.mips(s, ss) > 0) cout << "MWC hit s=" << s << " ss=" << ss << endl;
\endcode

\see \ref page_sttriggerdetectorcollection
\see \ref page_stctbtriggerdetector
*/
